# Aggregate Functions with HAVING

Display cities having an average score greater than 85.

```sql
SELECT City,
AVG(Score) AS AverageScore
FROM Student
GROUP BY City
HAVING AVG(Score) > 85;
```

---

Display cities having more than 2 students.

```sql
SELECT City,
COUNT(*) AS TotalStudents
FROM Student
GROUP BY City
HAVING COUNT(*) > 2;
```

---

Display cities whose total score is greater than 250.

```sql
SELECT City,
SUM(Score) AS TotalScore
FROM Student
GROUP BY City
HAVING SUM(Score) > 250;
```

---

# Multiple Aggregate Functions

```sql
SELECT
COUNT(*) AS TotalStudents,
SUM(Score) AS TotalScore,
AVG(Score) AS AverageScore,
MAX(Score) AS HighestScore,
MIN(Score) AS LowestScore
FROM Student;
```

---

# Aggregate Functions with GROUP BY

```sql
SELECT
City,
COUNT(*) AS TotalStudents,
SUM(Score) AS TotalScore,
AVG(Score) AS AverageScore,
MAX(Score) AS HighestScore,
MIN(Score) AS LowestScore
FROM Student
GROUP BY City;
```

